This is an impressive set of tools you've developed for automated file intelligence and network data analysis. Since you have a strong focus on backend development, library troubleshooting, and creating comprehensive documentation, this README is designed to be as professional and technical as the scripts themselves.Below is a structured description you can use to build your GitHub README.Project Overview: File Hunter & Search Intelligence SuiteThis repository contains a collection of advanced, multi-threaded Python engines designed for automated network intelligence and file discovery across the surface and dark web. These tools automate the extraction of metadata, file categorization, and recursive crawling of major file-hosting platforms.🛠 Core CapabilitiesAsynchronous Engines: Utilizes asyncio and aiohttp for high-concurrency crawling and concurrent task management.Multi-Engine Search: Supports automated queries across Google, Bing, Brave, Yahoo, Yandex, and DuckDuckGo.Recursive Deep-Crawling: Intelligent link extraction to navigate through file-hosting directories to find buried assets.Dark Web Integration: Includes built-in support for Tor SOCKS5 proxies to facilitate .onion search and discovery.Automated Metadata Extraction: Custom extractors for platforms like MediaFire and KrakenFiles to identify file sizes, types, and hashes.📂 Included ModulesScriptPrimary FunctionKey Featuresfile_hunter.pyFull-featured CLI DashboardSQLite caching, Rich UI, Tor integration, and deduplication.file_search_engine.pyAdvanced File IndexerElasticsearch indexing, VirusTotal scanning, and proxy rotation.file_search.pyLive Result MonitorReal-time Rich table updates and keyword frequency analysis.search_file.pyLightweight Meta-ExtractorSingle-script edition optimized for rapid metadata harvesting.🚀 Technical StackLanguage: Python 3.xLibraries: BeautifulSoup4, aiohttp, SQLAlchemy, psycopg2, cryptography, pygameStorage: SQLite3 (local caching) and PostgreSQL (via SQLAlchemy)UI: Rich and PyQt5 for graphical and terminal-based dashboards📜 UsageThe scripts are designed with a focus on automation and modularity.Initialize Environment: Setup your virtual environment and install dependencies.Execute Hunt: Run the interactive menu to select search engines and crawl depth.Analyze: Results are automatically exported to results.csv, results.json, or the local SQLite archive.